      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6a",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 791869251,
      "version": 137,
      "versionNonce": 2118069357,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784837772463,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Begin by assuming that good-enough? and improve operations are available as primitives.\nThen show how to expand these in terms of arithmetic operations. Describe each version\nof the sqrt machine design by drawing a data-path diagram and writing a controller definition\nin the register-machine language.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Begin by assuming that good-enough? and improve operations are available as primitives.\nThen show how to expand these in terms of arithmetic operations. Describe each version\nof the sqrt machine design by drawing a data-path diagram and writing a controller definition\nin the register-machine language.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "9Vb2um0O_0dwGhAaq0VWh",
      "type": "text",
